{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954530-experimenting-with-an-unusual-chronicle-format-feedback","id":954530,"title":"Experimenting with an unusual chronicle format. Feedback?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-20T12:01:52-07:00","id":954530,"title":"Experimenting with an unusual chronicle format. Feedback?","content":"I'm in the brainstorming stages for a Promethean chronicle, and I want to get some practical feedback and suggestions about how this would work at the table and what I should modify or change. Big picture: I want to run an anthology story that jumps around in time and the PCs might not play consistent characters. This probably wouldn't be a long-running chronicle, so I feel comfortable doing more specific planning and experimenting with the format.<br /> <br /> The basic inspiration here is the Canterbury Tales, mixed with the flashback emphasis of Mummy: the Curse. I'm imagining a frame story where the PCs are gathered together near the end of their various Pilgrimages, seemingly strangers, sharing their Rambles around a campfire. The main gameplay would involve them talking about their experiences, framed in terms of Milestones they attempted. &quot;Did I ever tell you about the time I tried to...&quot; So each session would be a flashback (or maybe several small ones in a session), presented as &quot;the first time I drove a car&quot; or &quot;confronting my creator&quot; or &quot;creating progeny&quot; or &quot;understanding the Psychopomp Role&quot; or whatever. By the end of the session, they would have either succeeded at the Milestone or conclusively failed at it, or maybe even died- the Pilgrimage goes on either way. I would be drawing these Milestones from ones the players provide to me ahead of time as things they'd want to explore in play and are open to succeeding or failing. What's cool about this is the story that ends up being told for a flashback could be &quot;about&quot; something very different from the stated Milestone- a PC might even die, as death is not the end for Prometheans. <br /> <br /> So that's the basic idea. Now, one way I could play this would be for the PCs to be a branded throng that's been with each other all along, and they play their own characters in every flashback and advance chronologically. That could be fun!<br /> <br /> Another option would be that each flashback has the primary Milestone-teller playing their own Promethean character, and other PCs are given temporary character sheets to represent other important characters in that flashback- another Created, a human ally, another supernatural, or maybe their own main character if they're crossing paths. This would be drawing on the troupe play ideas from Mummy (or Ars Magica), where each player has their main PC, a recurring companion for each other PC's narrative, and the option of some temporary lesser &quot;grog&quot; character to fill out a scene. Maybe the main PC would be the only one to receive accumulated Experiences, no matter who's being played. I would love to hear from anyone with practical experience doing troupe play in CofD here.<br /> <br /> Now here's the third option, and it's the thing I'm really excited about, but also scared of getting wrong or confusing my players. I really like running weird gonzo stuff with unusual formats as an ST and poking at what's real for the characters and what's imagination or just narrative convenience, and generally expecting things to be less grounded and more loose. But I've had mixed results when I try to do that, sometimes the players enjoy that, other times they end up a bit lost or confused. So I'd like to get some ideas on presenting this coherently.<br /> <br /> This would be something along the lines of The Years of Rice and Salt, where characters are reincarnated throughout the novel as different people but have recognizable personality traits and similar names each time, or Blackadder which does something similar for laughs (which would be just fine here.) An anthology story with the same set of actors playing different but similar characters.<br /> <br /> Here's the bones of the idea. As with option 2, there's a main PC in each flashback, and other players play different supporting roles depending on the story. However, each player is using the same character sheet every time. Same skills, same Lineage, same Elpis/Torment, same underlying personality type and quirks, etc. They might be playing another Created, or a sublimatus, or a qashmal, or even a human, but they keep the same sheet, and in some broad sense from the audience's perspective, they are &quot;the same person&quot; even if they don't exactly share knowledge. Different forks of the same ego, in Eclipse Phase terms. [Actually, maybe I shouldn't have them play qashmallim or sublimati, since the Pilgrimage would never lead there and I want the suggestion that this is the same Created all along, just playing a different role.]<br /> <br /> Maybe they have one long-term Aspiration that's the same across characters, but their two short terms switch out depending on the flashback. I could also give them a pool of temporary XP based on their character: &quot;use 6 Experiences to buy Skills or Merits for this role only,&quot; or like &quot;you are a vampire: keep your powers but reflavor them, also you may regain Pyros by drinking blood, and sunlight counts as an Extreme Environment.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would love to incorporate Roles into this. The main PC in the flashback might be traveling with a fallen priest who serves as their Confessor, which in fact is another PC who's practicing Cobalus at that time, and being a Confessor is literally the Role they play in this current story- which they might diverge from or break character, or the PC might get stuck in a rut playing the same Role across multiple stories, etc. The Cool Thing I want from this is all the PCs being able to advance their own Pilgrimage by hitting milestones and fulfilling Roles even when they're &quot;someone else&quot;.<br /> <br /> The appeal of this last format is that the group can play with reality versus narrative in interesting ways. There's lots of stories like this that I love, especially in theatre: R&amp;G Are Dead, Pippin, Into the Woods, a recent production of Frankenstein where the actors playing Victor and the Creature switched roles every other night...I really like the trappings and peculiarities of theatre and I want to bring that vibe to my tabletop group.<br /> <br /> For example, one way I could play the frame story is that the PCs all happen to be in the presence of a mighty qashmal, who orders them to recount each of their Pilgrimages- and through some potent Numen, they're cast into a sort of dream state where they literally relive the flashback and the other PCs are inserted into the Roles played by other people originally. Making the Chronicle itself some kind of dream experience (but not &quot;all just a dream&quot; because these are things that DID happen, just relived and with consequences across characters).<br /> <br /> And then as we near the end of the Chronicle, the PCs will each have been fulfilling their own Roles and Milestones and spending Experiences as usual, and their Pilgrimage rating will increase, and we can see where they're each at with the New Dawn for the finale.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Is this making any sense? I want to get some feedback on whether any of these approaches sound fun or interesting or even practical before I press further. Should I scrap the whole thing and stick to a standard format? Would you play in a chronicle like this? Does it give you any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}